-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",246,{
[7841]="70047B46\n1\tDestroy supply tents in Lang Rhuven (total: 8)\030Destroy trebuchets in Lang Rhuven (total: 6)\tEasterling supply tents and trebuchets can be found in Lang Rhuven on the border of Dagorlad. You should destroy supply tents and trebuchets found in Lang Rhuven.\n2\tCompleted\tCaused much damage to the enemies at Lang Rhuven.\n",
[7842]="70047B41\n1\tDefeat Khatikhôl\030Defeat Dashat Khôz\tKhatikhôl and Dashat Khôz can be found in Lang Rhuven on the border of Dagorlad. You should defeat Khatikhôl and Dashat Khôz.\n2\tReturn to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[7843]="70047B40\n1\tDefeat the war-party entering Lang Rhuven\tA war-party will be entering Lang Rhuven from the eastern end of the encampment. You should defeat the war-party before they get to the camp.\n2\tStand your ground and defeat the war-party\tA war-party will be entering Lang Rhuven from the eastern end of the encampment. You should defeat the war-party before they get to the camp. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tReturn to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[7844]="7002F35B\n1\tDefeat gredbyg and rats at Langraf (total: 10)\tGredbyg and rats can be found at Langraf. Waldeg has asked you to venture within Langraf and clean out the gredbyg and rats found within.\n2\tTalk to Waldeg\tWaldeg is at Snowbourn. Waldeg will be pleased to hear you have helped to clean the gredbyg and rats out of Langraf.\n",
[7845]="7002FC24\n1\tPay your respects at the first tomb\030Pay your respects at the second tomb\030Pay your respects at the third tomb\tThe tombs can be found within Langraf. Waldeg has asked you to venture into Langraf, find the tombs of his ancestors, and honour them by kneeling before them.\n2\tTalk to Waldeg\tWaldeg is at Snowbourn. Waldeg will be pleased to hear that you honoured his ancestors and remembered their sacrifice.\n",
[7846]="7001938A\n1\tLight lanterns (total: 13)\tThere are lanterns along the path between Imlad Lalaith and Caras Galadhon. Wait for night fall, and then light them to help lead revellers to the feast. As part of the preparations for the evening feast, Galhíril would like you to light the lanterns that will lead the evening revellers to the banquet.\n2\tTalk to Galhíril at Imlad Lalaith\tGalhíril is at Imlad Lalaith. You should return to Galhíril with your report.\n",
[7847]="70054888\n1\tYou are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.\t\n2\tCollect sullied plates in the dungeons of Barad-dûr (total: 16)\tSullied plates can be found throughout the dungeons of Barad-dûr.\n3\tClean the plates in the Foul Larder's washing-tub\tA washing-tub can be found in the Foul Larder in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.\n4\tInspect the cleaned plates\tThe cleaned plates can be found in the Foul Larder in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.\n",
[7848]="70008853\n1\tReturn to Chieftain Torbok at the Grimwood Lumber-yard\030Collect Grimwood-roots (total: 10)\tRoots can be found upon the downed trees throughout the Grimwood and the saplings that sprout from the ground. You might also find them on the Leafcull-trees. Chieftain Torbok wants you to get lashings for the walls at the Grimwood Lumber-yard.\n",
[7849]="7003E6D1\n1\tBow before the ancient tree\030Find the ancient tree\tOne of Lassemista's favourite places was a great tree. Quickbeam believes bowing before it will honour his memory. The tree can be found in the north-east of Fangorn.\n2\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder what else would honour Lassemista's memory. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n3\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has thought of how he next wishes to honour Lassemista's memory. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n4\tSay bye to Wellinghall\030Find Wellinghall\tLassemista enjoyed long talks with Treebeard. Quickbeam believes saying good-bye to Wellinghall will honour his memory. Wellinghall can be found in west Fangorn.\n5\tReturn to Quickbeam to hear what he has to say\tQuickbeam needs to ponder what else would honour Lassemista's memory. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n6\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has remembered how he next wishes to honour Lassemista's memory. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n7\tLook around at the small island\030Find the small island\tQuickbeam and Lassemista used to watch the river from a small island. Quickbeam asked you to go there and have a look around. The island is in the river in the centre of Fangorn.\n8\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder what else would honour Lassemista's memory. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n9\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has remembered how he next wishes to honour Lassemista's memory. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n10\tShed a tear at Lassemista's Seed\030Lassemista's Seed is at Isengard\tQuickbeam wishes to honour Lassemista by showing he misses him with a single tear. Lassemista's seed has been planted at Isengard.\n11\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam will wish to speak to you about Lassemista. Quickbeam is at Derndingle.\n",
[7850]="70067F65\n1\tFind spare oars (total: 2)\030Collect pillaged rations (total: 4)\tBalidan has asked you to collect some spare parts for his escape. The parts can be found within Mâr Naphra's off-limits storage.\n2\tMeet with Balidan\tYou have successfully collected everything Balidan needs to make his escape. Deliver them to the meeting point. Balidan is waiting on the coast south-west of Mâr Naphra.\n",
[7851]="7006212E\n1\tFind and burn Einion's corpse\tDelun has asked you to find what's left of her friends in Gond Orchal and burn their bodies. They're somewhere north-west of Delun's location. You should start with Einion.\n2\tFind and burn Curig's corpse\tDelun has asked you to find what's left of her friends in Gond Orchal and burn their bodies. They're somewhere north-west of Delun's location. You should search for Curig next.\n3\tFind and burn Melwyn's corpse\tDelun has asked you to find what's left of her friends in Gond Orchal and burn their bodies. They're somewhere north-west of Delun's location. Melwyn is the last person you must find.\n4\tReturn to Delun outside of Gond Orchal\tThe remains of Delun's friends have been found. You should return to her location outside of Gond Orchal.\n5\tTalk to Muna\tYou returned too late. The stranger seems to have something to say to you.\n",
[7852]="7003792D\n1\tSharpen arrow-shafts (total: 8)\tArrow-shafts in need of sharpening can be found in the armoury in Grimslade. You should sharpen arrows to help defend the walls.\n2\tBring the arrows to Frithferth\tFrithferth can be found outside the Weapons Store-house in Grimslade. You should bring the arrows to Frithferth.\n",
[7853]="7003797D\n1\tGather root vegetables (total: 8)\tRoot vegetables can be found in the woods surrounding Grimslade in the south-eastern Westfold. You should collect root vegetables for the people of Grimslade, who fear to go into the dangerous woods themselves to look for food.\n2\tBring the roots to Éobert\tÉobert can be found in Grimslade near the food stores. You should bring the roots you gathered to Éobert.\n",
[7854]="7003797C\n1\tHunt game animals for meat (total: 6)\tGame animals can be found in the green plains of the Westfold. You should hunt game animals for food to bolster Grimslade's stores.\n2\tBring the meat to Éobert\tÉobert can be found in Grimslade near the food stores. You should bring the meat to Éobert.\n",
[7855]="70034D08\n1\tDefeat Laudh\tLaudh stands watch over Gárnoth's Farm from his make-shift command post on the southern side of the farm.\n2\tDefeat Laudh\tLaudh, Lieutenant of Núrzum, stands watch over Gárnoth's Farm from his make-shift command post on the southern side of the farm.\n3\tCompleted\tLaudh, Lieutenant of Núrzum, is no longer coordinating the Orcs in Gárnoth's Farm, and they are bound to drift into chaos soon.\n",
[7856]="7000D4E6\n1\tMinas Angos is a tower in Barad Gúlaran, south of Gath Forthnír. You must travel to Barad Gúlaran and defeat Laugi Goldentongue, the emissary of the Dourhands, inside Minas Angos. Brúnfair suggested you take allies.\t\n2\tTalk to Brúnfair\tBrúnfair is at Gath Forthnír, north of Barad Gúlaran. Having defeated Laugi Goldentongue, you should return to Brúnfair and tell him of your victory.\n",
[7857]="70014878\n1\tDefeat Gathrok\030Defeat goblins in Gamil Filik (total: 9)\tGathrok and his goblins are in Gamil Filik, south-east of the Deep Descent. Stíling has asked you to defeat Gathrok, a goblin-chieftain, and weaken his forces.\n2\tTalk to Stíling\tStíling is hiding just at the outskirts of Gamil Filik in the Silvertine Lodes. You should return to Stíling and tell him that you were able to defeat Gathrok.\n",
[7858]="7001CB11\n1\tScout the southern gate of Durbúrz-stazg\030Scout the eastern gate of Durbúrz-stazg\tDurbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion. Aemeldir has asked you to scout the gates of Durbúrz-stazg to determine which is the least guarded.\n2\tTalk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion\tAemeldir is at Echad Sirion, south of Durbúrz-stazg. You should return to Aemeldir with the results of your patrol.\n",
[7859]="70068341\n1\tCollect fatty crocodile viscera ([see journal]/8)\tTevurin explained that the fatty layer between the crocodile's skin is difficult to obtain, but used by the craftsmen to keep their crocodile hide specialties supple. He asked that you spend some time collecting the fatty layer of the crocodiles from along the shore south and east of the expedition encampment.\n2\tTevurin explained that the fatty layer between the crocodile's skin is difficult to obtain, but used by the craftsmen to keep their crocodile hide specialties supple. He asked that you spend some time collecting the fatty layer of the crocodiles from along the shore south and east of the expedition encampment.\t\n",
[7860]="7003E684\n1\tTalk to Glorfindel\tGlorfindel is outside the Last Homely House in Rivendell, near the waterfall. Elrond bade you speak with Glorfindel and obtain his aid against Ferndúr the Virulent.\n2\tTalk to Glorfindel to march against Ferndúr and his minions\tGlorfindel is outside the Last Homely House in Rivendell, near the waterfall. You should speak with Glorfindel when you are ready to march against Ferndúr and his minions.\n3\tTalk to Glorfindel\tGlorfindel is outside the Last Homely House in Rivendell, near the waterfall. You should speak with Glorfindel regarding the encounter with Ferndúr the Virulent.\n4\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is in his library on the top floor of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell. Glorfindel bade you return to Elrond and give a report of your encounter with Ferndúr.\n",
[7861]="70015E22\n1\tDefeat Zagâfum\tZagâfum, the leader of the wood-trolls can be found in the cave of Sâd Thareg, south of Gwingris. Lithuilas has instructed you to defeat Zagâfum.\n2\tTalk to Lithuilas at Gwingris\tLithuilas is at Gwingris, north of Sâd Thareg. You should return to Lithuilas with news of your victory.\n",
[7862]="7002F99F\n1\tEnter the Nink-hai camp and locate their leader\tExplore the Nink-hai camp along the mountain path east of Faldham. Langfrith has asked you to infiltrate the Orc camp and discover the leader of the tribe.\n2\tUse the horn to draw Dargum's attention and defeat Grazadh\tThe Nink-hai leader can be found at the end of the mountain pass in the mountains. Langfrith has asked you to infiltrate the Orc camp and defeat the leader of the tribe.\n3\tReturn to Langfrith and inform him of Dargum's escape\tLangfrith awaits outside the mead hall of Faldham. Langfrith will want to hear of the events that transpired with the Nink-hai leader.\n",
[7863]="70008757\n1\tDefeat Mayor Wat Mudbottom\tMake your way south along the Hoardale River to the village of Hoarhallow. Taskmaster Fikdag directed you to find and kill Mayor Wat Mudbottom, the leader of the rat-folk village.\n2\tTalk to Task-master Fikdag\tTaskmaster Fikdag is at Dâr-gazag. You stalked through the trails to the centre of Hoarhallow and struck down their leader. You should return to Taskmaster Fikdag with the news.\n",
[7864]="70034AB5\n1\tFind and defeat the White Hand Siege-leader\tAn Orc Siege-leader can likely be found in the woods of the northern Whitshaws where the Orc patrols are the thickest. You should defeat the leader of the patrolling White Hand sentries in the Whitshaws.\n2\tAn Orc Siege-leader can likely be found in the woods of the northern Whitshaws where the Orc-patrols are the thickest. You should defeat the captain of the patrolling White Hand sentries in the Whitshaws.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the White Hand Siege-leader in the Whitshaws, but as long as Núrzum roams unhindered, the enemy is a greater threat than the people of Wildermore can withstand.\n",
[7865]="7002EFF3\n1\tFind and defeat an Under-wall Captain in the Under-wall\tLeaders of the Moria Orcs can be found in the northernmost and southernmost side passages in the Under-wall. Isteron wants you to send a message to the Moria Orcs by challenging one of their leaders in battle.\n2\tTalk to Isteron\tIsteron is by the northernmost exit from the Under-wall. You have defeated a Moria Orc-leader and should return to tell Isteron of your success.\n",
[7866]="7000C38B\n1\tFind and defeat Zagh, Master of the Guard\030Find and defeat Farmak the Best Runner\030Find and defeat Dâgal the Observer\tThe goblin-leaders Zagh, Dâgal, and Farmak dwell within Goblin-town. Goblin-town lies to the north-east of Glóin's camp. Vighar Roadwalker has tasked you with hunting down and defeating several leaders within the depths of Goblin-town.\n2\tTalk to Vighar Roadwalker at Glóin's camp outside of Goblin-town\tVighar Roadwalker is at Glóin's camp in the Misty Mountains, just outside of Goblin-town. You found the goblin leaders throughout Goblin-town. Dâgal watched over the Orcs from Angmar, Zagh travelled the tunnels yelling at the guards, and Farmak was found running through the tunnels in search of intruders. Now that thay have been defeated, you should return to Vighar.\n",
[7867]="7005AAB3\n1\tDefeat Margzasht the Crusher\030Defeat Núlnazt the Keen-eyed\030Defeat Akúlog of the Hoarfrost\tWarlord Dushtalbúk's advisors should be defeated if you can find them within Shakhajât.\n2\tTalk to Molkha\tMolkha waits for your report about the warlord's advisors.\n",
[7868]="70009E7C\n1\tDefeat Bok\030Defeat Gasham\tGrothum, the goblin-village in Arador's End, lies to the north. One of the leaders there watches the road into the Isendeep, the other hides deep within the crags of the camp. Lieutenant Ingi's hatred for the goblins knows no bounds. He wishes you to target the leaders of the Snowreap tribe at Grothum and remove them from the area.\n2\tTalk to Lieutenant Ingi\tLieutenant Ingi is at Ost Ringdyr, south of Grothum. Fighting through the Snowreap village of Grothum you found and defeated the two goblin leaders, Bok and Gasham. Now you should return to Lieutenant Ingo for your reward.\n",
[7869]="70017523\n1\tDefeat Moria Guardian (total: 8)\030Defeat Moria Curse-shouter (total: 4)\030Defeat Crazed Globsnaga (total: 6)\tGuardians, curse-shouters, and fungal Orc bombs can be found in the Sixteenth Hall, north-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Odmar sent you to find and destroy the Orcs that he believes are leading this diseased incursion into the Sixteenth Hall.\n2\tReturn to Odmar at the Shadowed Refuge\tOdmar is in the Shadowed Refuge, south-west of the Sixteenth Hall. You fought valiantly against the infected Orcs of the Sixteenth Hall and defeated many guardians, curse-shouters and the Orcs bearing terrible fungus. You should now tell Odmar that you did as he bade.\n",
[7870]="7002C303\n1\tDefeat Nink-hai chieftains (total: 3)\tThe Nink-hai Orc-tribe can be found south-west of Odda's tent. Odda has asked you to remove the chieftains who are atop the tribe's chain of command.\n2\tTalk to Odda at his tent near the road\tOdda can be found near the road south of the Cuthstan. You have disrupted the Nink-hai chain of command, and Odda is awaiting your return.\n",
[7871]="70030836\n1\tDefeat Nîn-stazg's Warleader from Mordor\tThe Warleader of Nîn-stazg can be found deep within the Orc encampment of Nîn-stazg, south-east of Floodwend. You should defeat the Warleader of Nîn-stazg.\n2\tReturn to Radwig in Floodwend\tThane Radwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should tell Thane Radwig that the Warleader has been slain, which should bring some peace of mind to the young Thane.\n3\tSpeak with Etta\tEtta, mother of Thane Radwig, is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should speak with Etta.\n",
[7872]="7002C89D\n1\tFind and defeat Lanferth\tLanferth's tent is located deep within Hordfierd. Idmar has asked you to defeat Lanferth, leader of the brigands.\n2\tTalk to Idmar\tIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant. You should return to Idmar at once with news of your victory.\n",
})
